  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Preheat the oven to 220C, fan-forced. Line an oven tray with baking paper. Coarsely chop the cucumber. Thickly slice the capsicum and tomatoes. Cut the rolls into 2cm chunks. Coarsely chop the hazelnuts. Drain and rinse the lentils.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2164138/photos/large/99658_1-d284487831326338f8debfa68ecec91a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Toast bread: Put the bread on the lined tray, spray or brush with olive oil and season with salt and pepper. Bake for 6-7 mins until toasted.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2164139/photos/large/99658_2-354ef26c4aee4c15b38b5444e289ec5a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook capsicum and lentils: Meanwhile, heat 1 tsp olive oil in a medium frypan over medium heat. Cook the capsicum, stirring occasionally, for 3-4 mins until softened. Add the lentils, season with salt and pepper and cook, stirring, for 1 min or until warmed through. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2164140/photos/large/99658_3-16e31e513513aaae7159adbd66343ba3.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dress salad: Put 3 tsp olive oil, 3 tsp red wine vinegar, 1 tsp dijon mustard and 1 tsp sugar in a large bowl, season with salt and pepper and whisk to combine. Add the cucumber, tomato, rocket, toasted bread and capsicum mixture and toss to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2164141/photos/large/99658_4-d2cf8ee1577263da7cbc67d85e14459e.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the salad among bowls, scatter over the hazelnuts and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2164142/photos/large/99658_5-5b837c263fd362055f4bf8a50b7b4175.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Did you know?: Panzanella is a classic Italian salad based on tomato and bread. The bread soaks up the tomato juices and vinaigrette, giving it loads of flavour. Stale bread is used traditionally, but toasting fresh bread works well too.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2164143/photos/large/99658_6-3b0b7d58d1ba74b7cef99f4d3948ef51.jpeg"
    }
  ]
